,'assistant','<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user said \"hi\", so I need to respond appropriately. Since they\'re using the system, I should acknowledge their greeting and offer assistance. The context provided includes data for both the week and year-to-date.\n\nFirst, I should check if there are any notable trends or issues in the data. For the week, room reservations are 23 with 5 rejected, which is a 21.7% rejection rate. That\'s higher than the YTD 17.3%. Maybe that\'s a point to mention. The top department this week is Customer Support, which is different from the YTD top department, Administration. That\'s an interesting shift.\n\nVehicle trips are down 4.3% compared to last year, and there\'s a high number of rejected vehicle bookings (71) which seems really high. Wait, the total vehicle bookings YTD are 45, but rejected are 71? That can\'t be right. Wait, looking at the data again: under Vehicle bookings total, Rejected is 71. But total bookings are 45. That\'s impossible because rejected can\'t exceed total. Maybe there\'s a typo. The user might be confused, so I need to point that out as a data inconsistency. \n\nDeliveries are up to 101 this week, and guest visits are 87 this week. The YTD guest visits are 3620, which is a lot. The most booked room is Ruang Garuda, but this week it\'s N/A. Maybe the room wasn\'t booked this week, or data isn\'t captured yet. \n\nI should structure the response with the week\'s data first, then YTD. Highlight the key points: high rejection rate for rooms this week, the shift in top department, vehicle booking inconsistency, and maybe the high number of rejected vehicle bookings. Then suggest checking the vehicle data for errors and possibly reviewing the room booking process to reduce rejections. \n\nAlso, the user might need to know how to export data, but they didn\'t ask, so I don\'t mention it unless they ask. Keep the response concise, bullet points, and professional. Make sure to mention the data inconsistency clearly so the user is aware.\n</think>\n\nHalo! Berikut ringkasan statistik terkini (minggu ini dan tahunan):  \n\n**Minggu Ini (13–19 Juli 2026):**  \n- **Reservasi ruang:** 23 total (5 ditolak, 21.7% penolakan)  \n- **Top departemen:** Customer Support  \n- **Kunjungan tamu:** 87  \n- **Pengiriman barang:** 101  \n\n**Tahun 2026 (hingga 19 Juli):**  \n- **Reservasi ruang:** +102.5% vs tahun lalu, tetapi penolakan mencapai 17.3% (14 kasus)  \n- **Kunjungan tamu:** 3,620 total  \n- **Kendaraan:**  \n  - **Masalah data:** Jumlah penolakan kendaraan (71) melebihi total booking (45). Perlu diverifikasi ulang.  \n  - **Penurunan 4.3%** vs tahun lalu.  \n\n**Rekomendasi:**  \n1. Periksa konsistensi data penolakan kendaraan (71 > 45 total).  \n2. Tinjau proses penerimaan reservasi ruang untuk mengurangi penolakan.  \n\nGunakan tombol ekspor PDF/CSV di header chat untuk unduh laporan lengkap.',NULL,'2026-07-17 21:37:17'),(31,10,'user','I want to ask',NULL,'2026-07-17 21:38:02'),(32,10,'assistant','Of course! Please provide more details about your request so I can assist you better.','{\"room\":{\"meeting_title\":null,\"room_id\":null,\"room_name\":null,\"booking_type\":null,\"online_provider\":null,\"department\":null,\"historical_user\":null,\"date\":null,\"number_of_attendees\":null,\"start_time\":null,\"end_time\":null,\"special_notes\":null},\"vehicle\":{\"vehicle_id\":null,\"vehicle_name\":null,\"plate_number\":null,\"borrower_name\":null,\"department\":null,\"date_from\":null,\"date_to\":null,\"start_time\":null,\"end_time\":null,\"purpose\":null,\"destination\":null,\"purpose_type\":null}}','2026-07-17 21:38:03'),(33,12,'user','what you can do',NULL,'2026-07-17 21:38:13'),(34,12,'assistant','Sorry, the AI service returned an error. Please try again later.','{\"room\":[],\"vehicle\":[]}','2026-07-17 21:38:13'),(35,11,'user','What i can do with this?',NULL,'2026-07-17 21:38:32'),(36,11,'assistant','<think>\nOkay, the user is asking \"What I can do with this?\" after I provided the summary data. Let me think about how to respond.\n\nFirst, I need to understand their intent. They might be looking for actionable steps based on the data I\'ve given. Since they\'re part of the facility management system at Kebun Raya Bogor, they probably want to optimize operations or improve efficiency.\n\nLooking at the data: Room reservations have a high rejection rate (17.3%) this year, which is a problem. The most booked room is Ruang Garuda, but this week there\'s no most booked room. Vehicle bookings have a slight decrease compared to last year, and there\'s a high number of rejected vehicle bookings. Deliveries and guest visits are up, but there are pending documents for deliveries.\n\nPossible actions: Address the high rejection rate by reviewing the approval process. Maybe streamline the criteria or provide feedback to departments. For vehicle bookings, the high rejection rate (71 out of 45 total?) Wait, that doesn\'t add up. Wait, the vehicle bookings total is 45, but rejected is 71? That can\'t be right. Wait, looking back at the data: Vehicle bookings total is 45, but rejected is 71. That\'s impossible because rejected can\'t exceed total. Wait, maybe there\'s a typo. Let me check the original data again.\n\nOriginal data says for 2026 year-to-date: Vehicle bookings total: 45 (vs 47 last year, -4.3%). Rejected: 71. That\'s a mistake. Wait, maybe the numbers are split differently. Wait, maybe the user made a typo. Let me check again. The user provided:\n\nVehicle bookings total : 45 (vs 47 last year, -4.3%)\n  Pending              : 2\n  Approved/Ongoing     : 3\n  Rejected             : 71\n  Today\'s trips        : 5\n\nWait, that\'s impossible. If total bookings are 45, how can rejected be 71? That\'s a data inconsistency. Maybe it\'s a typo. Perhaps the rejected is 7, not 71. But as per the given data, I have to work with what\'s there. But that\'s a problem. However, since I can\'t question the data, I need to proceed. Maybe it\'s a mistake in the data entry. But I have to use the numbers as provided.\n\nSo, for vehicle bookings, the rejection rate is 71/45, which is over 100%, which is impossible. That\'s a red flag. The user might need to check data accuracy. But since I can\'t point that out directly, maybe I can suggest reviewing the data entry process for vehicle bookings.\n\nOther points: High pending documents for deliveries (43 pending). Maybe improve delivery documentation processes.\n\nFor room bookings, the top department is Administration, but this week it\'s Customer Support. Maybe there\'s a shift in usage patterns. Also, the peak booking hour is 17:00-18:00, which is late. Maybe adjust booking hours or encourage earlier reservations.\n\nRecommendations could include:\n\n1. Investigate the high rejection rate in vehicle bookings (though the numbers don\'t add up, but proceed as per given data).\n2. Streamline room booking approvals to reduce rejections.\n3. Address pending delivery documents to avoid delays.\n4. Monitor the shift in top departments for room bookings.\n\nAlso, the user might need to export the data for further analysis. But according to the instructions, I should mention the export buttons instead of suggesting workarounds.\n\nSo, the response should highlight the key issues, suggest actions, and mention the export options if needed.\n</think>\n\nHere are actionable steps based on the data:\n\n1. **Reduce Room Booking Rejections**  \n   - **Issue**: 17.3% rejection rate (14/81) year-to-date.  \n   - **Action**: Review rejection reasons (e.g., scheduling conflicts, documentation gaps) and streamline approval workflows for high-priority departments like Administration.  \n\n2. **Address Vehicle Booking Anomalies**  \n   - **Issue**: Vehicle bookings show **71 rejected** out of 45 total (likely a data inconsistency—verify accuracy).  \n   - **Action**: Audit vehicle booking records for errors and clarify rejection criteria to avoid over-rejection.  \n\n3. **Optimize Delivery Documentation**  \n   - **Issue**: 43 pending delivery documents.  \n   - **Action**: Assign a dedicated team to prioritize and clear pending documents daily.  \n\n4. **Monitor Room Usage Shifts**  \n   - **Trend**: Customer Support (this week) vs. Administration (year-to-date) as top departments.  \n   - **Action**: Analyze if resource allocation (e.g., Ruang Garuda) should shift to meet evolving departmental needs.  \n\n**Export Data**: Use the **PDF/CSV export buttons** (next to the trash icon) to analyze trends in Excel or share with stakeholders. Let me know if you need further insights!',NULL,'2026-07-17 21:38:35'),(37,12,'user','today schedule',NULL,'2026-07-17 21:38:58'),(38,12,'assistant','Today\'s approved room meetings: [ID:691] \'meeting bersama pomsty\' in Ruang Merak (Customer Support), [ID:697] \'testing on going page lagi\' (online via Google Meet, Finance), and [ID:696] \'testing on going\' (online via Google Meet, Customer Support). Approved vehicle trips: [ID:982] \'jalan jalan\' with Honda Vario (B 2169 MVX) for Administration (17 Jul 22:28–02 Aug 14:28) and [ID:981] \'meeting bersama ponsty\' with Carry PickUp (B 8024 FGV) for Executive (17 Jul 22:06–17 Jul 23:07).','{\"room\":{\"meeting_title\":null,\"room_id\":null,\"room_name\":null,\"booking_type\":null,\"online_provider\":null,\"department\":null,\"historical_user\":null,\"date\":null,\"number_of_attendees\":null,\"start_time\":null,\"end_time\":null,\"special_notes\":null},\"vehicle\":{\"vehicle_id\":null,\"vehicle_name\":null,\"plate_number\":null,\"borrower_name\":null,\"department\":null,\"date_from\":null,\"date_to\":null,\"start_time\":null,\"end_time\":null,\"purpose\":null,\"destination\":null,\"purpose_type\":null}}','2026-07-17 21:39:01'),(39,12,'user','how bout the vehicle',NULL,'2026-07-17 21:39:22'),(40,12,'assistant','Sorry, the AI service returned an error. Please try again later.','{\"room\":[],\"vehicle\":[]}','2026-07-17 21:39:22'),(41,12,'user','halo',NULL,'2026-07-17